  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup> <mi>x</mi> <mrow> <mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mi>x</mi> </mfrac> </mrow> </msup> <mo>&#8658;</mo><msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup> <mi>x</mi> <mrow> <mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mi>x</mi> </mfrac> </mrow> </msup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mtext>ln</mtext><mi>x</mi></mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mi>x</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math><br />At <math> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </math> and sign change of derivative is from positive to negative, hence <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></math> is a point of local maxima of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br />Now <math><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, hence <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> or <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is the greatest element of set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math></p><p>Since <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math><br />So, <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math> is the largest element of set <math><mi>P</mi></math></p>",
